#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=S. L. Linnea {{quote-gloss|pseudonym; Sharon Linnéa; Barbara K. Sherer}}|chapter=January 27, 2007, 12:10 {{smallcaps|p.m.}}|title=Treasure of Eden|series=Eden Thrillers|seriesvolume=3|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:St. Martin's Press|St. Martin’s Paperbacks]]|pages=281–282|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/treasureofeden0000linn/page/282/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-312-94216-8|passage=His sons sensed that he was not a great man; he was no one who would have become Hajj under normal circumstances. He belonged with the other '''unremarkables''' in the middle of the pack.}}
